// Olympiad strategies: ten ways of thinking, each with a question that starts the search, the idea, a solved example,
// a ladder of problems (Madagascar selection, Pan-African, international level) with progressive hints and full
// solutions, and the experiments and challenges of the site where the idea can be handled. Bilingual (owner rule:
// Olympiad is its own category, French and English). Maths between \( \) or \[ \]. Problems are classical ones restated
// in our own words; a credit names a competition only where the problem comes from one.
